<!-- rtdf-document-id: sara/section63 -->

> Module Section63
> Using Definitions as W
> Using Section2 as S2
> Using Section68 as S68
> Using Section151 as S151

```catala-metadata
declaration scope TaxableIncome:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input period content W.TaxPeriod
  filing scope S2.FilingStatusFor
  exemptions scope S151.PersonalExemptions
  limitation scope S68.ItemizedDeductionLimit
  output gross_income content money
  output adjusted_gross_income content money
  output itemized_deductions content money
  output standard_deduction content money
  output personal_exemptions content money
  output taxable_income content money
```

```catala
declaration itemizes content boolean
  depends on world content W.World,
             taxpayer content W.Entity
  equals
    (exists election among
       (W.status_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.ItemizeDeductions)
     such that W.same_entity of election.identifier, taxpayer)
    or (exists deduction among
          (W.financial_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Deduction)
        such that W.has_agent of deduction, taxpayer)

declaration is_nonresident_alien content boolean
  depends on world content W.World,
             person content W.Entity,
             period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals exists event among
           (W.status_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.NonresidentAlien)
         such that W.has_agent of event, person
                   and W.overlaps_period of event.starts, event.ends, period

declaration spouse_itemizes content boolean
  depends on world content W.World,
             spouse content optional of W.Entity
  equals match spouse with pattern
         -- Absent: false
         -- Present content person:
              exists deduction among
                (W.financial_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Deduction)
              such that W.has_agent of deduction, person
```

§63. Taxable income defined

(a) In general

Except as provided in subsection (b), for purposes of this subtitle, the term "taxable income" means gross income minus the deductions allowed by this chapter (other than the standard deduction).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0003; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(a); source-lines: 3-5; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope TaxableIncome:
  definition filing.world equals world
  definition filing.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition filing.period equals period
  definition gross_income equals
    let own equals W.gross_income_individual of world, taxpayer, period in
    match filing.spouse with pattern
    -- Absent: own
    -- Present content spouse:
        if filing.status = S2.FilingStatus.JointOrSurviving
        then own + (W.gross_income_individual of world, spouse, period)
        else own
  definition adjusted_gross_income equals gross_income
  definition exemptions.world equals world
  definition exemptions.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition exemptions.period equals period
  definition exemptions.adjusted_gross_income equals adjusted_gross_income
  definition limitation.world equals world
  definition limitation.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition limitation.period equals period
  definition limitation.adjusted_gross_income equals adjusted_gross_income
  definition limitation.itemized_deductions equals
    raw_itemized of world, taxpayer, period
  definition itemized_deductions equals limitation.allowed
  definition personal_exemptions equals exemptions.total
```

(b) Individuals who do not itemize their deductions

In the case of an individual who does not elect to itemize his deductions for the taxable year, for purposes of this subtitle, the term "taxable income" means adjusted gross income, minus-


```catala
scope TaxableIncome:
  definition taxable_income equals
    let deductions equals
      if itemizes of world, taxpayer
      then itemized_deductions + personal_exemptions
      else (nonitemizer_standard_component of standard_deduction)
           + (nonitemizer_personal_exemption_component of personal_exemptions) in
    if adjusted_gross_income <= deductions
    then $0
    else round of (adjusted_gross_income - deductions)
```

    (1) the standard deduction, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0005; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(b)(1); source-lines: 11-11; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration nonitemizer_standard_component content money
  depends on standard_deduction content money
  equals standard_deduction
```

    (2) the deduction for personal exemptions provided in section 151.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0006; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(b)(2); source-lines: 13-13; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration nonitemizer_personal_exemption_component content money
  depends on personal_exemptions content money
  equals personal_exemptions
```

(c) Standard deduction

For purposes of this subtitle-


```catala
declaration standard_deduction_under_subsection_c content money
  depends on basic_amount content money,
             additional_amount content money
  equals basic_amount + additional_amount
```

    (1) In general

    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term "standard deduction" means the sum of-


```catala
scope TaxableIncome:
  definition standard_deduction equals
    let temporary_increase equals special_2018_2025_rule of period in
    let status equals marital_status_for_section63 of filing.status in
    let basic equals
      basic_standard_deduction of status, temporary_increase in
    let taxpayer_additional equals
      (aged_or_blind_count of world, taxpayer, period)
      + (if is_aged of world, taxpayer, period then 1 else 0) in
    let spouse_additional equals
      match filing.spouse with pattern
      -- Absent: 0
      -- Present content spouse:
          if status = S2.FilingStatus.JointOrSurviving
             or (status = S2.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
                 and (W.gross_income_individual of world, spouse, period) = $0)
          then (aged_or_blind_count of world, spouse, period)
               + (if is_aged of world, spouse, period then 1 else 0)
          else 0 in
    let ineligible equals
      ineligible_for_standard_deduction of
        (married_separate_spouse_itemizes of status,
           (spouse_itemizes of world, filing.spouse)),
        (is_nonresident_alien of world, taxpayer, period), false in
    let additional equals
      additional_standard_deduction of status,
        (taxpayer_additional
         + (if temporary_increase then 0 else spouse_additional)) in
    standard_deduction_after_ineligibility of ineligible,
      (standard_deduction_under_subsection_c of basic, additional)
```

        (A) the basic standard deduction, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0009; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(1)(A); source-lines: 23-23; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration basic_component content money
  depends on basic_standard_deduction content money
  equals basic_standard_deduction
```

        (B) the additional standard deduction.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0010; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(1)(B); source-lines: 25-25; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration additional_component content money
  depends on additional_standard_deduction content money
  equals additional_standard_deduction
```

    (2) Basic standard deduction

    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-


```catala
declaration basic_standard_deduction content money
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus,
             temporary_increase content boolean
  equals match status with pattern
    -- S2.FilingStatus.JointOrSurviving:
        if temporary_increase
        then 2 * temporary_other_basic_amount
        else joint_or_surviving_basic_amount
    -- S2.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold:
        if temporary_increase
        then temporary_head_of_household_amount
        else head_of_household_basic_amount
    -- S2.FilingStatus.Unmarried:
        if temporary_increase then temporary_other_basic_amount
        else other_basic_amount
    -- S2.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately:
        if temporary_increase then temporary_other_basic_amount
        else other_basic_amount
```

        (A) 200 percent of the dollar amount in effect under subparagraph (C) for the taxable year in the case of-


```catala
declaration joint_or_surviving_basic_amount content money
  equals 200% * other_basic_amount
```

            (i) a joint return, or


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0013; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(2)(A)(i); source-lines: 33-33; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration joint_return_uses_joint_basic_amount content boolean
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus
  equals status = S2.FilingStatus.JointOrSurviving
```

            (ii) a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0014; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(2)(A)(ii); source-lines: 35-35; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration surviving_spouse_uses_joint_basic_amount content boolean
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus
  equals status = S2.FilingStatus.JointOrSurviving
```

        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0015; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(2)(B); source-lines: 37-37; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration head_of_household_basic_amount content money
  equals $4400
```

        (C) $3,000 in any other case.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0016; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(2)(C); source-lines: 39-39; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration other_basic_amount content money
  equals $3000
```

    (3) Additional standard deduction for aged and blind

    For purposes of paragraph (1), the additional standard deduction is the sum of each additional amount to which the taxpayer is entitled under subsection (f).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0017; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(3); source-lines: 41-43; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration additional_standard_deduction content money
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus,
             qualifying_circumstances content integer
  equals (additional_amount_per_circumstance of status)
         * qualifying_circumstances
```

    (5) Limitation on basic standard deduction in the case of certain dependents

    In the case of an individual with respect to whom a deduction under section 151 is allowable to another taxpayer for a taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the individual's taxable year begins, the basic standard deduction applicable to such individual for such individual's taxable year shall not exceed the greater of-


```catala
declaration dependent_basic_standard_deduction_cap content money
  depends on earned_income content money
  equals
    let earned_income_amount equals dependent_earned_income_amount of earned_income in
    if dependent_floor_amount >= earned_income_amount
    then dependent_floor_amount
    else earned_income_amount
```

        (A) $500, or


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0019; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(5)(A); source-lines: 49-49; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration dependent_floor_amount content money
  equals $500
```

        (B) the sum of $250 and such individual's earned income.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0020; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(5)(B); source-lines: 51-51; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration dependent_earned_income_amount content money
  depends on earned_income content money
  equals $250 + earned_income
```

    (6) Certain individuals, etc., not eligible for standard deduction

    In the case of-


```catala
declaration ineligible_for_standard_deduction content boolean
  depends on separate_spouse_itemizes content boolean,
             nonresident_alien content boolean,
             nonindividual_entity content boolean
  equals separate_spouse_itemizes or nonresident_alien or nonindividual_entity
```

        (A) a married individual filing a separate return where either spouse itemizes deductions,


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0022; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6)(A); source-lines: 57-57; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration married_separate_spouse_itemizes content boolean
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus,
             spouse_itemizes content boolean
  equals status = S2.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately and spouse_itemizes
```

        (B) a nonresident alien individual, or


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0023; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6)(B); source-lines: 59-59; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration nonresident_alien_ineligible content boolean
  depends on nonresident_alien content boolean
  equals nonresident_alien
```

        (D) an estate or trust, common trust fund, or partnership,


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0024; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6)(D); source-lines: 61-61; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration nonindividual_entity_ineligible content boolean
  depends on is_estate_or_trust_or_fund_or_partnership content boolean
  equals is_estate_or_trust_or_fund_or_partnership
```

    the standard deduction shall be zero.


```catala
declaration standard_deduction_after_ineligibility content money
  depends on ineligible content boolean,
             otherwise_allowable content money
  equals if ineligible then $0 else otherwise_allowable
```

    (7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025

    In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026-

    Paragraph (2) shall be applied-


```catala
declaration special_2018_2025_rule content boolean
  depends on period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals period.tax_year >= 2018 and period.tax_year <= 2025
```

        (i) by substituting "$18,000" for "$4,400" in subparagraph (B), and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0027; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(7)(i); source-lines: 71-71; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration temporary_head_of_household_amount content money
  equals $18000
```

        (ii) by substituting "$12,000" for "$3,000" in subparagraph (C).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0028; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(7)(ii); source-lines: 73-73; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration temporary_other_basic_amount content money
  equals $12000
```

(d) Itemized deductions

For purposes of this subtitle, the term "itemized deductions" means the deductions allowable under this chapter other than-


```catala
declaration raw_itemized content money
  depends on world content W.World,
             taxpayer content W.Entity,
             period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals
    Money.sum of
      (combine all deduction among
         (W.financial_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Deduction)
       in amounts initially []
       with if W.has_agent of deduction, taxpayer
               and W.overlaps_period of deduction.starts, deduction.ends, period
            then amounts ++ (W.weighted_amounts of deduction)
            else amounts)
```

    (1) the deductions allowable in arriving at adjusted gross income, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0030; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(d)(1); source-lines: 79-79; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration itemized_after_above_line_exclusion content money
  depends on chapter_deductions content money,
             adjusted_gross_income_deductions content money
  equals
    if chapter_deductions <= adjusted_gross_income_deductions then $0
    else chapter_deductions - adjusted_gross_income_deductions
```

    (2) the deduction for personal exemptions provided by section 151.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0031; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(d)(2); source-lines: 81-81; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration itemized_after_personal_exemption_exclusion content money
  depends on deductions_before_exclusion content money,
             personal_exemptions content money
  equals
    if deductions_before_exclusion <= personal_exemptions then $0
    else deductions_before_exclusion - personal_exemptions
```

(f) Aged or blind additional amounts

    (1) Additional amounts for the aged

    The taxpayer shall be entitled to an additional amount of $600-


```catala
declaration aged_or_blind_count content integer
  depends on world content W.World,
             taxpayer content W.Entity,
             period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals
    combine all event among
      ((W.personal_status_events of world)
       ++ (W.employment_and_institution_events of world))
    in count initially 0
    with if (event.kind = W.EventKind.Blindness
             or event.kind = W.EventKind.Retirement)
            and W.has_agent of event, taxpayer
            and W.overlaps_period of event.starts, event.ends, period
         then count + 1 else count
```

        (A) for himself if he has attained age 65 before the close of his taxable year, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0033; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(1)(A); source-lines: 89-89; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration is_aged content boolean
  depends on world content W.World,
             person content W.Entity,
             period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals exists event among (W.relationship_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Birth)
         such that W.has_agent of event, person
           and exists born among event.starts
               such that period.tax_year - (Date.get_year of born) >= 65
```

        (B) for the spouse of the taxpayer if the spouse has attained age 65 before the close of the taxable year and an additional exemption is allowable to the taxpayer for such spouse under section 151(b).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0034; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(1)(B); source-lines: 91-91; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration spouse_aged_additional_allowed content boolean
  depends on spouse_is_aged content boolean,
             spouse_exemption_allowed content boolean
  equals spouse_is_aged and spouse_exemption_allowed
```

    (2) Additional amount for blind

    The taxpayer shall be entitled to an additional amount of $600-


```catala
declaration blind_additional_amount content money
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus,
             blindness_circumstances content integer
  equals (additional_amount_per_circumstance of status)
         * blindness_circumstances
```

        (A) for himself if he is blind at the close of the taxable year, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0036; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(2)(A); source-lines: 97-97; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration is_blind content boolean
  depends on world content W.World,
             person content W.Entity,
             period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals exists event among (W.status_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Blindness)
         such that W.has_agent of event, person
                   and W.overlaps_period of event.starts, event.ends, period
```

        (B) for the spouse of the taxpayer if the spouse is blind as of the close of the taxable year and an additional exemption is allowable to the taxpayer for such spouse under section 151(b).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0037; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(2)(B); source-lines: 99-99; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration spouse_blind_additional_allowed content boolean
  depends on spouse_is_blind content boolean,
             spouse_exemption_allowed content boolean
  equals spouse_is_blind and spouse_exemption_allowed
```

    For purposes of subparagraph (B), if the spouse dies during the taxable year the determination of whether such spouse is blind shall be made as of the time of such death.


```catala
declaration spouse_blind_at_relevant_time content boolean
  depends on blind_at_year_end content boolean,
             blind_at_death content boolean,
             spouse_died_during_year content boolean
  equals if spouse_died_during_year then blind_at_death else blind_at_year_end
```

    (3) Higher amount for certain unmarried individuals

    In the case of an individual who is not married and is not a surviving spouse, paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be applied by substituting "$750" for "$600".


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0039; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(3); source-lines: 103-105; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration additional_amount_per_circumstance content money
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus
  equals
    if status = S2.FilingStatus.Unmarried then $750 else $600
```

(g) Marital status

For purposes of this section, marital status shall be determined under section 7703.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0040; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(g); source-lines: 107-109; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration marital_status_for_section63 content S2.FilingStatus
  depends on status_determined_under_section_7703 content S2.FilingStatus
  equals status_determined_under_section_7703
```
